<title>CANADA: Falconbridge in Dominican labor talks.</title>
<headline>Falconbridge in Dominican labor talks.</headline>
<dateline>TORONTO 1996-11-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Falconbridge Ltd said it is negotiating a new labor contract with its employees in the Dominican Republic.</p>
<p>A three-year agreement with 1,000 of the 1,500 employees at Falconbridge Dominicana ends on Saturday, a Falconbridge spokeswoman said.</p>
<p>If no agreement is reached by then, local regulations require a mandatory period of conciliation before a strike or lockout are allowed, she said.</p>
<p>In 1995, the facility produced 30,900 tonnes of nickel in ferronickel.</p>
<p>--Reuters Toronto Bureau 416 941-8100</p>
</text>
